## 11. 4-Minute Demo Script

### Setup

- **4 devices** on table: Phone 1 (Field Responder), Phone 2 (Gateway), Phone 3 (Citizen), Phone 4 (Citizen/Victim)
- Phones 1, 3, 4 in **Airplane Mode** (BLE + Wi-Fi re-enabled)
- Phone 2 has internet (Gateway)
- Laptop showing Command Center dashboard

### Script

| Minute | Action | What Judges See |
|---|---|---|
| **0:00–1:00** | Show Airplane Mode on Phones 1, 3, 4. On **Phone 4**: press Volume Down 3× — feel the haptic pulse. | 🔴 Volume SOS sent silently. "This victim is trapped in the dark." |
| **1:00–2:00** | Hold Phone 4 near Phone 3 → Phone 3 near Phone 1. | SOS **hops** across the mesh. Appears on Field Responder's map as red dot with GPS. |
| **2:00–3:00** | Phone 1 (Field Responder) near Phone 2 (Gateway). Point to laptop. | SOS appears on **Command Center dashboard**. Click the pin → type *"Rescue team dispatched, ETA 20 min"* → send ACK. |
| **3:00–4:00** | ACK flows: Dashboard → Firebase → Gateway → Mesh → Phone 4. Show Phone 4's screen. | Victim sees: **✅ "Rescue team dispatched, ETA 20 min"**. A legacy phone connects to Phone 1's hotspot `EMERGENCY_CONNECT_HERE`, opens browser portal, sees bulletins. |

### Closing Line

> ***"Four phones. Zero internet. A victim trapped in the dark pressed a button three times, and 60 seconds later, a rescue team was dispatched from a command center 500 kilometers away. When everything fails, Bridgefy doesn't."***

---

## 12. Judge Q&A — Prepared Answers

| Question | Answer |
|---|---|
| *"Fake SOS spam?"* | Hardware-fingerprinted rate limit (1 per 2 min). Field responders can mute devices. |
| *"Battery drain?"* | BLE is ~10mW. Auto Power Saver at 30%, Emergency Beacon at 15% — survives 6–8 hrs on minimal battery. |
| *"Fake government alerts?"* | Ed25519 cryptographic signatures. Private key never leaves Command Center. Even decompiling the app yields only the public key. |
| *"How does data reach a remote govt facility?"* | Gateway node auto-activates on internet. Batches mesh data → Firebase. Dashboard reads in real-time. Bulletins flow back the same path. |
| *"What about people without smartphones?"* | Captive Portal. Any device with Wi-Fi + browser connects to `EMERGENCY_CONNECT_HERE` hotspot. Zero download. |
| *"Scale?"* | Max 10 hops + 24hr TTL + delta-sync (only missing messages). Network stays lean at hundreds of nodes. |
| *"GPS indoors?"* | Falls back to last known GPS. Volume SOS + Dead Man's Switch still send location. Manual address entry available. |
| *"What if no one moves?"* | Each phone is a relay. Messages propagate as people move naturally — the mesh is "carried" by human movement. In static scenarios, Wi-Fi Direct range (~200m) still covers a building. |
| *"Cost?"* | Entire stack is free and open-source. ₹0 infrastructure cost. |
| *"iOS support?"* | Android first — best BLE/Wi-Fi Direct support. iOS users connect via Captive Portal (no app needed). Native iOS port is future scope via MultipeerConnectivity. |

---

## 13. Known Risks & Mitigations

| Risk | Probability | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| BLE discovery flaky during demo | Medium | Have a **backup screen recording**. Also test in the exact demo room — BLE interference varies. |
| Android OEM kills ForegroundService | Medium | Exempt app from battery optimization on demo phones. Test on actual devices early. |
| Captive portal redirect doesn't auto-trigger | Medium | Fallback: tell user to open browser → `192.168.49.1`. |
| Firebase quota exceeded | Low | Demo won't hit 50K reads. But have offline-only fallback ready. |
| Nearby Connections API version incompatibility across phones | Low | Use same Android version on all demo phones if possible. Test cross-device early. |

